                     "topFinding":  "Six findings closed this run, the first real movement in four runs, and every one of them landed in the release and guard layer rather than on a page. push-to-github.ps1 gained a -Path parameter with a pathspec-scoped add and commit, a staged-file secret-shape gate with an explicit override, and .gitignore gained a sixteen-pattern secret-shaped-filename block; release.ps1 now re-runs check-status-json.ps1 after its own Step 2 writer; collect-usage.ps1 caps the published queue payload at 60 rows. What did not move is the thing that has not moved in nineteen runs: deploy-pages.yml was re-read line by line again and still carries no delete step, so the served .work-queue.json answers 200 at 1,475,763 bytes on both yesandeverything.com and raw.githubusercontent.com, up from 1,118,496 two days ago, and the live queue went 444 to 600 items. Health is 75, up from 74, and the verdict holds at working: no hard rule is breached, both gates are intact, all five worker routes answer, and every public property returns 200. The next thing to do is unchanged and now cheaper than it was, because the pathspec plumbing the untrack step needed already exists.",
